cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the authors using the information below.
  Reviewer: Julian (Tiki) Gonzalez, U.S. Army Corps of Engineers, Risk Management Center
  (https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9058-7653). This repository is under active review and development.
type: software
title: "BestFit-Python-Examples"
version: "0.2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/USACE-RMC/BestFit-Python-Examples"
license: 0BSD
url: "https://github.com/USACE-RMC/BestFit-Python-Examples.git"
abstract: >-
  Twelve notebooks follow the saved RMC-BestFit application examples using frozen source data,
  visible model settings, and a shared plotting package. They cover flood frequency, information
  expansion, dependence, coincident frequency, rating curves, time series, and regression.
keywords:
  - BestFit
  - pythonnet
  - MCMC
  - optimization
  - probability distributions
  - fitting
  - analysis
  - bayesian
  - flood frequency
  - estimation
